    description: "WHAT. The inherited-calls linker binds a call to the first same-named method it meets on the receiver type's MRO and ignores overloads. tapir: Tapir.fileBody calls rawBinaryBody(..).map(_.file)(d => ..), the curried two-list map. On dev it bound EndpointTransput.map (line 51, right); once Scala dotted parents are recorded (PR #2329) EndpointTransput.Atom becomes reachable and the call binds EndpointTransput.Atom.map (line 100, the one-parameter override): wrong. One call of 7 gained on tapir.\n\nASK. Choose among same-named candidates by arity / parameter-list shape where the call site shows it, as overload_arity does elsewhere; leave a tie unresolved or flagged rather than taking the first.\n\nFound during PR #2329 (2026-11-22). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md and RESIDUALS_TO_FILE.md."  # 26ae
